socho tumne naya ghar liya। Khali ghar। Ab har cheez khud banaaoge? Sofa khud banaaoge? Fridge khud banaaoge? AC khud banaaoge?

Nahi na — baazar se ready made laoge। Sofa furniture shop se, fridge electronics shop se।"
Programming mein yahi NPM hai। Node.js tumhara khali ghar hai। NPM — baazar hai। Doosre developers ke banaye hue packages — ready made furniture hain।"
Aaj NPM seekhenge — aur professional folder structure bhi। Chalte hain

PART 1 — NPM KYA HAI 

NPM — Node Package Manager। Teen words — teen meanings 

N — Node      → Node.js ke liye
P — Package   → Ready made code bundles
M — Manager   → Install, update, remove
                karna manage karta hai

Matlab — Node.js ke liye ready made code bundles ko manage karne wala tool।

Package — ek bundle hai code ka। Kisi doosre developer ne ek problem solve ki — code likha — NPM pe upload kar diya — ab duniya use kar sakti hai।"


"Example — password encrypt karna। Do options
 <!--password -> 123456  -->
 <!-- encrypted password -> ASDF234234@#$%@#$% -->

Option 1 — Khud banao:
Cryptography padho
Algorithms samjho
Code likho
Bugs fix karo
Test karo
→ 3 mahine ka kaam

Option 2 — NPM se lo:
npm install bcrypt
→ 30 seconds

Yahi NPM ki power hai। Duniya ke developers ne problems solve ki हैं — tumhe dobara solve nahi karni

NPM Registry — baazar

NPM Registry — ek badi online library hai। Abhi — 2 million se zyada packages hain।"
Jaise Amazon pe lakho products hain — NPM pe lakho packages hain। Tum order karo — tumhare project mein install ho jaata hai।


PART 2 — PACKAGE.JSON

Folder analogy

Hospital          →  Backend Project

Reception         →  routes/
(Kahan jaana hai    (Request kahan
 batata hai)         jaayegi batata hai)

Doctors           →  controllers/
(Actual kaam        (Actual logic
 karte hain)         yahan hoti hai)

Patient Records   →  models/
(Data store         (Database schema
 hota hai)           yahan hota hai)

Security Guard    →  middleware/
(Entry check        (Request verify
 karta hai)          karta hai)

Control Room      →  config/
(Sab settings       (Database connection,
 yahan hain)         env variables)